==[[Range/Lore|The Range's lore assets]]==
===[[Range/Lore/EP4|Episode 4]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone13.mp3}} "[[Brimstone]], I do not understand. Our secrets were buried deep. But [[Fade|a blackmailer]] has everything. They did not leak our [[VALORANT Protocol#The Blackmailer's agent dossiers|dossiers]] to the public, but they could, and they will. [[Cypher]] has rivals, but they are not behind this. He claims the work is too impressive, and if Cypher's impressed, we should all be very concerned. You need to put the [[Omega]] plans on hold. We are far too exposed to fight a war on both fronts. This blackmailer is the priority now. We need them found... or dead."
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone15.mp3}} "Commander, the strike team to apprehend this [[Fade|blackmailer]], you asked for my recommendations. Besides myself, we must send [[Cypher]]. No one else can handle surveillance of an entire city. [[Chamber]] can provide fire support from a vantage position. [[Breach]] has a... history with extractions, it would be foolish not to take advantage. [[Neon]] can help cover ground quickly. Also, she needs a break from [[Killjoy]]. Those two have been cooped up in the lab for too long. And [[KAYO|KAY/O]] has agreed to pilot the VLT/R. Five on the ground, one in the skies, this is good. We will bring this threat to justice, Brimstone. You have my word."
*{{AC|file=KAYO Audio Log Istanbul Mission Complete.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/EP4#Cypher's_Office|Range/Lore/EP4 → v4.07 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone24.mp3}} "Commander, I return with good news. A rarity these days, but, no less welcome. My mission to Alpha Lisbon was a success by two measures. First, [[Killjoy]]'s invention worked without incident. The dimensional radiometer can calculate the [[Alpha]]-[[Omega]] mesh with a two percent margin of error. Extraordinary!... or so I am told. Killjoy ran off shouting before I was given a better explanation, huh. Second, the readings confirm our projections. The [[radianite]] fabric on our side is strong. There is no imminent danger of Omega breaching this location. We can relocate our defenses to more vulnerable sites. I would suggest S43, but that is a contentious point at best. I look forward to my next assignment. Until then."

===[[Range/Lore/EP5|Episode 5]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone41.mp3}} "Commander, please accept my sincerest apologies. In my zealousness I may have set the danger room to... slightly above the recommended safety limit. Uh, as a result, I have received a non-life-threatening injury which I can assure you will not interrupt my duties. I'm on the way to medical as we speak. Once I am treated I will ensure that the blood on the floor is cleaned. It is a slipping hazard, and for this, again, I apologize. Speak to you soon."

===[[Range/Lore/EP9|Episode 9]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone92.mp3}} "Brimstone! Brimstone, pick up! Listen, something's happened! The containment cell has been smashed open by [[Vyse|whatever]] was inside, there's metal everywhere, and I can't turn these alarms off! Brimstone, get over here now!"

===[[Range/Lore/V26|Season 2026]]===
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap2.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 5|Range/Lore/V26 → v12.04 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap3.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 6|Range/Lore/V26 → v12.05 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap4.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 7|Range/Lore/V26 → v12.06 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap6.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 9|Range/Lore/V26 → v12.08 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap8.mp3}} "[[Omega Viper|Commander]], this couldn't wait. The operation was a success, by more than our typical measures! α-[[Sage]]'s abilities are compromised. We confirmed it at 0820 and it matches the combat data from last week. This is the result we've been fighting for! With Sage no longer a factor, we can advance our plans into the next phase. Congratulations! We're lifting off in two minutes, see you soon!"
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap11.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 14|Range/Lore/V26 → v13.01 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap12.mp3}} "Yes, thank you, Doctor, it's fine. Uh, I know she can't respond, I'll only be a moment... yes, yes, go on ahead... Hello, [[Omega Sage|Sage]]. I'd rather let you dream peacefully in there but... who else will listen to my insufferable conscience. [[Omega Omen|Omen]] says hello, by the way. He's working on the matching hat. When you get out, don't forget to wear it around the base. He'll be... well, I'm sure he'll be his version of happy. Things are... things are not well. [[Omega Viper|Sabine]] claims she's fighting for you but... her anger, it's eaten up everything else. We need you home, out of these damn chemicals! Cruel of me to ask but it's true! We need your kindness! Your compassion! You are the one who held us back from our worst instincts, I see that now. I'll do what I can in your absence, I owe you that much. Keep feeling better, my friend. Doctor!... I'm okay, thank you..."
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone134.mp3}} "You need to speak with [[Cypher]] and [[Fade]]. We're staking too much on this wiretap. I admit they're skilled hackers but it's not their primary expertise. There will be breaches they won't detect. It's not a question of if this bites us, but when. The longer we leave it open, the greater the risk Omega can use it against us. For all we know, maybe they already have. Please, talk to them. So that when the time comes, they're ready to shut it down."
*{{AC|file=LegionAudioTap14.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/V26#Cypher's Office 17|Range/Lore/V26 → v13.05 → Cypher's Office]].)''

